# Voltfeld — which unit sits inside which.
# Inferred from the `member-of` frontmatter of every unit (units/ and work-systems/):
# Voltfeld ⊃ Portfolio · Charger ART ⊃ three product lines (⊃ two teams each) and three FL1 work systems · Hardware Engineering ·
# Software Engineering · Operations ⊃ Manufacturing, Supply Chain · Commercial ⊃ Sales,
# Field Service. The two engineering departments are empty boxes on purpose — their
# people are members of the ART teams. `layout: tree` draws the same containment as a tree.
# `around` + `radius` scope the picture to this organization (the index spans the whole
# workspace): `up: 0` = nothing above the company root, `down: inf` = everything inside it.
mode: infer
layout: nested
around: "[[Voltfeld]]"
radius: { up: 0, down: inf }
notes:
  - on: "[[Supply Chain]]"
    text: "Not in the ART; 14-week tooling lead time"
